  "original_hypotheses": [
    "N is any positive integer with trivial nebentypus. The index runs through every native Γ₀(N) cusp via the orbit of the signed primitive rows. Both integral frames receive their actual width normalization.",
    "Physical critical parameter s=1/2+it, every t∈ℝ, every spatial point in the upper half-plane; y>0 for all normalized observation horocycles.",
    "Every character dilation uses a primitive character χ mod q and q²B|N. The conductor-one ordinary family includes the two original completed constant terms. The uncompletion reciprocal is used as nonzero only off t=0."
  ],
  "removed_premises": [
    "Both opposed physical residue sets at fixed lower-left c>0 are put in finite bijection modulo their distinct observing widths; Γ₀ membership gives uniqueness. This pays the initial entry symmetry entering critical adjointness.",
    "Meromorphic uniqueness and conjugation of the normalized positive original seeds prove the actual continued entries are symmetric and satisfy critical entrywise Schwarz reflection, including t=0.",
    "The signed paired-divisor change χ→χ⁻¹ and native even K order reconstruct the original complete reflection including negative frequencies. The genuine conductor-one completed field carries both zero-mode terms. The exact ordinary scale is shown nonzero at t≠0 from the Gauss, gamma and L factors.",
    "The actual oldform-to-cusp forward equality at q²B|N continues to Re(s)≥1/2, s≠1. With the earlier Cramer inverse and ordinary reflection it places every true E_a(t) in the physical E_b(−t) span for every t≠0, without any assumed matrix or completeness.",
    "The unit-period measurements of that actual finite equality at every y>0 have coefficients determined by evaluation and differentiation at y=1. This proves the physical functional equation and reflected inverse matrix product off zero. Native parameter regularity extends both to t=0; symmetry and Schwarz reflection identify the reflected matrix with the adjoint and give both products exactly."
  ],
  "remaining_full_premises": [
    "Actual global continuous orthogonal resolution on the spatial quotient, including its residual constant, the full test pairing and Plancherel normalization; when using spatial truncation the all-cusp finite-part/Maass–Selberg bridge is still outstanding.",
    "Complete normalized four-spectrum trace, the physical manuscript Bessel test/inversion, holomorphic basis and all oldform Hilbert norms and native Maass Hecke compatibility.",
    "Full ABL/Pascadi Theorem A plus J and regular/ordinary-large-sieve bounds on the exact coefficient families and common phase; original Kim–Sarnak bound/exceptional gap and the true 7/32 energy, zero-frequency corrections and final Eq24."
  ],
  "classification": "Source-level genuine native scattering and functional-equation mechanism, classical omitted formal machinery. It supplies no counterexample to the manuscript. All checks are source-only, pending authorized kernel verification.",
  "independent_review": {
    "reviewer": "T10",
